  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN.\nYou can perform the following operation on the array:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N)(1 \\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N);\nChoose a set of indices SSS of size KKK, (1≤K≤N,1≤Sj≤N)(1 \\le K \\le N, 1\\le S_j \\le N)(1≤K≤N,1≤Sj​≤N);\nSet Ai=AS1⊕AS2⊕AS3⊕…⊕ASKA_i = A_{S_1}\\oplus A_{S_2}\\oplus A_{S_3}\\oplus \\ldots \\oplus A_{S_K}Ai​=AS1​​⊕AS2​​⊕AS3​​⊕…⊕ASK​​, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\nLet BBB denote the array obtained after sorting the array AAA. Your task is to convert the array AAA to array BBB using **at most** ⌈3⋅N2⌉\\lceil {\\frac{3\\cdot N}{2}} \\rceil⌈23⋅N​⌉ operations.\n\nYou also need to print the operations performed to convert the array AAA to array BBB. If there are multiple ways to convert the array, print any.\n\nIt is guaranteed that there exists at least one possible solution.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN, the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers, the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print (2⋅M+1)(2\\cdot M + 1)(2⋅M+1) lines:\n\n\n\nOn the first line, print MMM, the number of operations required to convert the array AAA to array BBB, where (0≤M≤⌈3⋅N2⌉)(0\\le M \\le \\lceil {\\frac{3\\cdot N}{2}} \\rceil)(0≤M≤⌈23⋅N​⌉).\nDescribe each operation in two lines:\n\nIn the first line, print two space-separated integers iii and KKK  (1≤i,K≤N)(1\\le i,K \\le N)(1≤i,K≤N), the chosen index and the number of elements in the set SSS.\nIn the second line, print KKK space-separated integers, the elements of set SSS. Note that all elements of the set SSS should be **distinct**.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤30001 \\leq T \\leq 30001≤T≤3000",
      "2≤N≤10002 \\leq N \\leq 10002≤N≤1000",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 600060006000."
    ],
